  "assessment": [
    "Seven of eight historical seat source blobs match. The remaining character-record-consumer.js change only accepts and forwards initialAssets while loading the avatar. Motion, room bind/capture/restore/removeActor and controller creation/disposal semantics are preserved.",
    "Per-group publication preflight runs before replacement. A rejected preflight leaves displayed actors and their seat leases live. A successful switch cancels the previous batch and disposes displayed actors; disposeRecordController releases the instance lease before disposal of motion/avatar resources. After successful preflight the new batch retains historical per-record failure behavior.",
    "Render-resource changes concern verified initial bytes, per-document embedded bitmap ownership and reference counting of shared body normal textures. Live skeletons, roots, behavior tasks and lease tokens remain per instance. Facility restore stages actors and restores their signed revision and pose before replacing the prior idle roster.",
    "Technical recommendation: the reviewed 241ce compiled closure supports a supplemental seat-v1 declaration for the pinned plant transfer. The observed first incompatibility is the absent declared contract. Production authority decides registration.",
    "Coverage boundary: CPU published-room replay used the historical built-in signed pair. The prior same-build public-batch-a/b motion receipts and mixed ordinary-game reception are complementary, but do not exercise that mixed pair against the published company seat. Exact mixed contact/visuals, GPU behavior, independent acceptance and standing-vocal contracts are outside this result."
  ],
  "testContext": "Fixed checkout A ran the navigation/lease subset. For the historical published-room test and resource/host tests the full main checkout supplied the headless adapter and fixture files omitted by the sparse checkout. Git compared all listed tracked source/fixture paths to the frozen commit; no differences. No browser or rendering.",
